The reported fault — that VLAN 5 (10.5.0.0/24) and VLAN 6 (10.6.0.0/24) hosts on switch4 lost their uplink to the multilayer switch gateway after maintenance — does not exist in the live lab. Direct probes across all five affected end-hosts (pc1, pc2, dc_pc5 on VLAN 5; pc3, pc4 on VLAN 6) show 0% packet loss to their respective gateways, 10.5.0.254 and 10.6.0.254, both of which are SVI addresses hosted on sshswitch's br_v5 and br_v6 bridge instances.

The trunk between switch4 (eth0) and sshswitch (eth0) is correctly configured on both side
